   "textKind": "explain",
   "content": "**India, Pakistan and Ethiopia have the most out-of-school children and young people:** about **48 million**, **21 million** and **19 million**. The largest numbers:\n\n- **India:** 47.6 million (2026)\n- **Pakistan:** 21.4 million (2025)\n- **Ethiopia:** 19 million (2025)\n- **Bangladesh:** 9.2 million (2025)\n- **Tanzania:** 7.6 million (2024)\n\nThe map sizes each country's circle by its number; hover a circle for the figure. Each country's latest figure from 2020–2026; primary and secondary school age, both sexes. Source: UIS, November 2026 release; indicator OFST.1T3.CP.",
